00:23:27.680 --> 00:23:29.960
They've colonized this place, Zebra.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:32.920
Zavadovsky Island, just off the Antarctic coast.

00:23:36.450 --> 00:23:40.650
Covered in bare rock, it's exactly what chinstraps need for nesting.

00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:46.870
Of course, being so close to Antarctica, it ought to be covered in snow and ice.

00:23:47.940 --> 00:23:50.780
But Zavadovsky is a hot, active volcano.

00:23:53.470 --> 00:23:58.430
The penguins have their own centrally heated island with easy access to krill.

00:24:04.730 --> 00:24:06.570
Two million breed here.

00:24:07.170 --> 00:24:09.970
It's the largest chinstrap colony in the world.

00:24:18.840 --> 00:24:21.180
The penguins that breed the farthest south,

00:24:21.600 --> 00:24:25.180
actually on the Antarctic continent, are the Adelis.

00:24:25.680 --> 00:24:27.400
And between them and their colony

00:24:27.400 --> 00:24:29.710
are miles and miles of spring.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:35.160
sea ice, which means weeks of walking.

00:24:36.820 --> 00:24:39.580
The trip is longer than many the emperors have to make,

00:24:39.970 --> 00:24:41.230
perhaps 60 miles.

00:24:41.820 --> 00:24:45.880
Nevertheless, in white bib and black tails, they set off.

00:25:02.590 --> 00:25:02.710
Thank you.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:44.030
At least it's spring, and the Adelis don't have to walk to their colony in the dark of winter.

00:25:46.860 --> 00:25:52.180
Eventually they reach it, a patch of bare rock and pebbles on an Antarctic hillside.

00:25:53.340 --> 00:25:58.450
The sweeping wind, hurricane force sometimes, keeps the rocks free of snow.

00:26:02.240 --> 00:26:04.300
The summer this far south is short.

00:26:04.740 --> 00:26:07.500
Most families will be ready to leave in three months.

00:26:09.100 --> 00:26:09.840
Most of them.

00:26:11.690 --> 00:26:14.890
But Adelis live just inside the margins of possibility.

00:26:18.280 --> 00:26:22.300
